cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "In-Hand Reorientation with the XHand1"
abstract: >-
  Reinforcement learning for in-hand object reorientation on a 12-DoF RobotEra XHand1
  dexterous hand. A PPO policy trained in Isaac Lab across 4096 parallel environments
  flips a two-face sponge 180 degrees in an upturned palm and holds it, reaching 70%
  hold success under full domain randomization, and replays without retraining on a
  Franka-mounted variant of the same hand.
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Fang
license: MIT
keywords:
  - dexterous manipulation
  - in-hand reorientation
  - reinforcement learning
  - Isaac Lab
  - sim-to-real
